@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Security & Privacy Architecture";
}

<div class="custom-card p-5 mx-auto" style="max-width: 800px;">
    <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-3"><i class="bi bi-shield-check text-primary me-2"></i>Security &amp; Data Integrity Architecture</h2>
    <p class="text-muted">This web application has been engineered as a university graduation project adhering to industry security best practices:</p>

    <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-3 my-4">
        <div class="p-3 bg-light rounded-3">
            <h6 class="fw-bold mb-1"><i class="bi bi-person-lock text-primary me-2"></i>1. Resource-Level Ownership Verification</h6>
            <p class="small text-muted mb-0">Every operation performed by a Seller or Customer strictly validates resource ownership on the server side using the authenticated user identity claims. No client-supplied ID parameters are trusted blindly.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-3 bg-light rounded-3">
            <h6 class="fw-bold mb-1"><i class="bi bi-arrow-repeat text-success me-2"></i>2. Atomic Checkout &amp; Anti-Overselling Transactions</h6>
            <p class="small text-muted mb-0">Order placement is encapsulated within database transactions with RepeatableRead isolation. Live stock levels are validated immediately before decrementing inventory, preventing race conditions and overselling.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-3 bg-light rounded-3">
            <h6 class="fw-bold mb-1"><i class="bi bi-file-earmark-lock text-warning me-2"></i>3. Secure File Uploads with Magic Byte Inspection</h6>
            <p class="small text-muted mb-0">Uploaded product images undergo strict MIME validation, extension whitelisting, file size restrictions (2MB), and binary magic signature inspection to thwart disguised executable payloads.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-3 bg-light rounded-3">
            <h6 class="fw-bold mb-1"><i class="bi bi-shield-shaded text-info me-2"></i>4. CSRF, XSS &amp; Overposting Defenses</h6>
            <p class="small text-muted mb-0">Every state-changing POST endpoint is protected by anti-forgery validation tokens. Dedicated ViewModels prevent parameter overposting, and Razor HTML encoding protects against cross-site scripting.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <a asp-action="Index" class="btn btn-primary-custom">
        <i class="bi bi-arrow-left me-1"></i>Back to Home
    </a>
</div>
